    "explanation": "This is about the SGD 4.50 cancellation fee charged after DRV-09712 cancelled trip TRP-02712 at 12:34:59 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, and both of you have ended up asking for the same thing: a full refund of that fee, with no payment to the driver.\n\nThe driver's own GPS trace, EV-GPS-02712, is the decisive measurement. It runs 91 fixes at a 10-second cadence with 100% coverage and no gaps, so it is complete and unimpaired for the arrival and dwell tests (POL-NS-08(b) is not engaged). Across the whole trace the driver never came closer than 258.2 m to the pickup pin (derived.driver_track.min_distance_m) and he recorded zero fixes inside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE arrival radius (derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count = 0). POL-NS-02's arrival test therefore fails and POL-NS-01 limb (b) cannot be met, so the SGD 4.50 is not chargeable. The effective in-geofence dwell is 0 seconds against the 180-second free waiting period in force for this trip (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec), a shortfall of 180 seconds, so POL-NS-06 independently produces the same result. The driver's own concession that he never entered the radius is accepted.\n\nThe clause that governs the facts is POL-NS-03. The driver's closest approach of 258.2 m, where he waited out the 4.4-minute wait shown in the trip record, is outside the 120 m arrival radius but inside the 400 m ceiling, while the rider's own track (EV-GPS-02712 rider_track; all 54 fixes within 19.9 m of the pin and stationary) places her at the pickup point. On fault allocation, the rider's chat message at 12:30:56 (EV-CHAT-02712) named her entrance - 'im at the main entrance next to the taxi stand, block A' - and the driver did not move to it before cancelling, so under POL-NS-03(i) the driver bears the loss and receives no compensation.\n\nI reject the rider's POL-NS-05 argument that the 'I'm Here' tap was a false arrival marker. POL-NS-05 bites where the trace puts the driver more than 300 m from the pin at the marker, or shows him travelling at 15 km/h or more at it; what the trace shows is a closest approach of 258.2 m, within 300 m, and the record does not establish the driver at or above 15 km/h at the 12:30:36 marker. POL-NS-05 expressly sends a driver who is stationary within 300 m of the pin, but outside the arrival radius, to POL-NS-03. No false-arrival referral is therefore recorded.\n\nI reject the rider's POL-NS-04 argument. Limb (b) requires the driver to have neither replied within 120 seconds nor placed an in-app call; the driver replied 'ok' at 12:31:26, 30 seconds after the rider's message, so POL-NS-04 does not apply on its own terms and the residual mislocation falls to be decided under POL-NS-03.\n\nThe driver's claim to SGD 3.60 is rejected. POL-NS-07 compensates only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, and limb (b) fails; POL-NS-03(i) then allocates the loss to the driver. No pin-ambiguity goodwill arises either: the rider did specify her entrance and registered_pickup_points is 1, so POL-NS-03(ii) does not apply. The anti-farming check does not trip (no_show_terminations_30d of 1 against 92 completed trips in 30 days, a rate of about 0.011, well under 0.08), so nothing is withheld on that ground.\n\nNo escalation ground is met. The trace, chat and fare records are complete and consistent (the SGD 4.50 cancellation-fee line equals the net figure produced by the resolution rule, platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd = 4.50), the parties share no no-show history, and the only missing artifact, the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02712-01, carries no deciding fact here: it goes only to POL-NS-06(i), which the driver could not have used in any event because he recorded no in-geofence interval.\n\nThe figures used are SGD 4.50 charged to the rider (fare_breakdown.cancellation_fee and total_charged, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00) and SGD 4.50 refunded. No driver compensation is payable. The monetary effect of SGD 4.50 is below the SGD 8.00